{"extract": "Prakash Keshav Javadekar (born 30 January 1951) is an Indian politician and former parliamentarian. He served as the Minister of Environment, Forest and Climate Change two times, from May 2014 to July 2016 and from May 2019 to July 2021.\nJavadekar was elected to the upper house Rajya Sabha as a Member of Parliament from Maharashtra in 2008, and re-elected from Madhya Pradesh in 2014.\nFollowing the victory of the Bharatiya Janata Party in the 2014 Indian General Election, he was appointed Minister State (Independent Charge) for Environment, Forests and Climate Change by Prime Minister Narendra Modi. He was also a Minister of State for Parliamentary Affairs, and briefly held the portfolio of Information and Broadcasting.\nJavadekar is an official spokesperson of the BJP.", "links": [{"ns": 10, "title": "Template:Infobox officeholder", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "2014 Indian General Election", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Ajay Sancheti", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Anil Madhav Dave", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Anurag Singh Thakur", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Arun Jaitley", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Arvind Sawant", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Bharatiya Janata Party", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Bhupender Yadav", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Dharmendra Pradhan", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Faggan Singh Kulaste", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Harsh Vardhan (Delhi politician)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "India", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Madhya Pradesh", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Maharashtra", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Maharashtra Legislative Council", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Mahendra Nath Pandey", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Manish Tewari", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Medha Kulkarni", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Member of Parliam